Z/2 * Z                            def= 1 h2(Y;rho)=1 h1(G;rho)=1  [x order 2, rho(x)=-1] -> consistent
Z/2 x Z                            def= 0 h2(Y;rho)=1 h1(G;rho)=0  [x order 2] -> consistent
one-relator <x,a|w^2>              def= 1 h2(Y;rho)=1 h1(G;rho)=1  [w order 2, rho(w)=-1] -> consistent
(Z/15 x| Z/2) * Z                  def= 1 h2(Y;rho)=1 h1(G;rho)=1  [x order 2] -> consistent
Z/2 * Z/2 * Z                      def= 1 h2(Y;rho)=1 h1(G;rho)=1  [x order 2] -> consistent
A *_{Z/3} (identity HNN)           def= 0 h2(Y;rho)=1 h1(G;rho)=0  [a^5 order 3, rho=zeta^2] -> consistent
Z/6 *_{Z/2} Z/6 *_{Z/3} (3 rels)   def= 0 h2(Y;rho)=1 h1(G;rho)=0  [a^3 order 2, rho=-1] -> consistent

Paper's group G (6 relators, 04-construction.tex l.14-27):
G = P/K (6-relator presentation)   def=-1 h2(Y;rho)=2 h1(G;rho)=0  [x1 order 2, rho=-1] -> consistent
Cor 2.4 + h1(G;rho)=0 would force every finite 2-complex Y with pi_1=G to have chi(Y)>=1,
i.e. def(G) <= 0, whereas the 5-generator relation module is generated by r1..r4 (K_ab=0):
a relation gap  d_F(N) >= 5 > 4 >= d_G(N_ab)  -- not stated in the paper.

ALL CONSISTENT
